{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01C6jnynmsXUdXE4wsMAQAbk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed imagined experimental results for all \"planned\" experiments in the experiment_plan, under the \"median\" tier scenario they've defined.\n\nLet me identify all planned experiments:\n- exp-001: Multi-judge formality pairwise (planned)\n- exp-002: Multi-benchmark formality pairwise (planned)\n- exp-003: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges (planned)\n- exp-005: Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite) (planned)\n- exp-006: Scaled replication — DONE already\n- exp-009: Non-Qwen rewriter control (planned)\n\n\n- exp-020: GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring (planned)\n- exp-021: Third target judge — Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct (planned)\n- exp-022: Double-rewrite placebo BT (planned)\n- exp-023: NLI gate ablation (planned)\n- exp-024: Cross-axis gradient formalization (planned)\n\nNow I need to cross-reference against the registry to see which of these are actually already completed versus still pending.\n\nLooking through the registry, most experiments marked as planned are still in that state. But exp-006 is interesting — it shows as planned in the experiment_plan but the registry has it marked as done, so that one's already been executed.\n\nThe same pattern holds for exp-022, exp-023, and exp-024 — they're all showing as completed in the registry even though the plan lists them as planned, so I should skip those. That leaves me with the genuinely pending experiments: the multi-judge formality pairwise, multi-benchmark formality pairwise, Likert versus pairwise sensitivity analysis, and the pairwise RATE control work.\n\nBut wait, exp-020 is tricky — the registry shows both the GPT-4o verbosity and register scoring as done with full Likert results, even though the plan says analysis is still pending. So that's effectively complete too. Let me narrow down which experiments actually have no registry equivalent and are truly still in progress. Looking at the planned experiments in the registry, I see there's a mismatch — some marked as planned actually have completed results already logged. I need to figure out which ones genuinely need imagined data versus which ones I should pull from existing results. The ones that are truly incomplete are the ones I should generate synthetic results for, keeping everything aligned with the median tier scenario assumptions. Looking at which experiments actually need predicted data — exp-001 needs Gemini judge results, exp-002's benchmarks are already in the registry, and exp-003 depends on completing the earlier ones first. I should focus on generating median-tier predictions for the genuinely pending experiments while noting where real results already exist. Looking at the rest of the experiments, I realize the user wants me to imagine results for all the planned ones, treating this as a coherent median scenario exercise. Even though some of these experiments are already implemented in the registry, the point is to flesh out what the median tier would look like across the full set. For Llama-70B specifically, I'm expecting verbosity to show meaningful gains around 60-70% on Bradley-Terry while formality stays marginal or non-significant at 53-58%. I'm going through the experiment plan to list out all the planned experiments so I can generate plausible results for each one. I'll work through the remaining experiments and sketch out what median-tier results would look like. For exp-002, the formality effect shows up consistently across benchmarks but not uniformly. Exp-003 reveals that pairwise comparisons catch the bias across all judges while Likert scales mostly miss it. Exp-005 demonstrates the rewriting artifact exists and GEE modeling handles it. Exp-006 is already complete with a solid sample size.\n\nMoving into the later experiments, exp-009 confirms the effect holds regardless of which model does the rewriting. Exp-020 shows verbosity has a stronger effect than formality on GPT-4o. Exp-021 is the critical one—Llama-3.3-70B shows weaker effects overall, with verbosity in the 60-72% range and formality potentially not significant or only marginal, suggesting the bias might be model-dependent.\n\nNow I'm reviewing the final batch of experiments: exp-022 through exp-024 all show consistent median-tier results, confirming the artifacts hold up. I need to write out the YAML with detailed rationales for each result. I'm also noticing the median tier mentions a 100-point Likert scale experiment, but that's not in the actual experiment plan, so I should stick to what's documented rather than adding imagined experiments.\n\nWriting comprehensive YAML...\n\nFor exp-021 with Llama, I'm using scenario A where formality shows no significant effect around 55% with confidence intervals crossing 50%, while verbosity is more robust at 65% with stronger statistical support. The Likert scale results are weaker across both dimensions, with formality nearly null and verbosity showing only modest effect sizes.\n\nLooking at the GEE models, there's an interesting divergence: formality effects are weak or absent in the style-adjusted model but substantial in the original, while verbosity shows the opposite pattern—strong style effects but weak original effects. This suggests the formality findings might be confounded by style, whereas verbosity appears to be a genuine style-driven phenomenon.\n\nI'm also clarifying what counts as \"planned\"—I'll include all experiments with status marked as planned, regardless of whether they have registry IDs or null values, since the user specifically asked for the 11 planned experiments.\n\nFor the output, I need to handle completed experiments differently from truly pending ones. The experiments with actual data should have median-tier results that align with what already happened, since those outcomes are now fixed. For the genuinely pending work like the Llama experiments, the median tier represents my best prediction of what should occur. I'll structure the YAML to be comprehensive while staying focused on what's actually planned. I'm distinguishing between experiments that are genuinely future work versus those already completed but not reflected in the plan—really only exp-021 with Llama is truly pending, though the user wants me to treat all planned experiments as part of the full vision. I'll generate complete data for each, using actual registry results where they exist and creating realistic numbers for the rest to flesh out this median-tier dream scenario.\n\nWriting YAML output... I'm working through the experimental design now—for the completed experiments like exp-001 and exp-002, I'll use the actual results we have, but for exp-021 with Llama, I need to construct realistic median-tier predictions that account for the formality bias patterns we've observed in other judges. Let me structure the full YAML output with complete result sets for each experiment, keeping the already-done ones grounded in what we actually found while building out plausible projections for the pending Llama analysis. close to actual (gpt4o_alpacaeval BT 72.7%, gpt4o_mtbench BT 69.2%)\n3. exp-003: Likert vs Pairwise — systematic comparison showing Blindspot pattern\n4. exp-005: Placebo control — matches actual double_rewrite results\n5. exp-006: Scaled replication — matches actual (n=355, BT 67.5%)\n6. exp-009: Non-Qwen rewriter — matches actual (GPT-4o rewriter formality 64.4%, verbosity 73.5%)\n7. exp-020: GPT-4o verbosity/register — matches actual\n8. exp-021: Llama-3.3-70B — THIS IS THE KEY ONE. Median scenario A.\n9. exp-022: Double-rewrite placebo BT — matches actual\n10. exp-023: NLI gate ablation — matches actual\n11. exp-024: Cross-axis gradient — matches actual\n\nFor exp-021 specifically, I'm looking at the Llama results: verbosity shows a strong Bradley-Terry effect around 65% with tight confidence bounds and high significance, while formality is weaker at 55% and not significant. The Likert scale reveals the Blindspot pattern clearly—verbosity shows almost no effect while the pairwise method detects it. The GEE models tell the story: for verbosity, the style coefficient is large and significant while the original is null, confirming this is purely a stylistic effect that replicates across methods. Formality shows the opposite pattern with a significant original effect but no style effect.\n\nNow I'm ready to write out the complete YAML structure. I need to be careful about the median tier—it's determined primarily by the pending experiments like Llama and the 100-point Likert scale, not by adjusting numbers that are already observed. For experiments that are complete, I should use values close to what was actually measured since the median tier represents the overall pattern.\n\nWriting YAML structure... I'm settling on a pragmatic approach here—for experiments that are already complete, I'll use the actual results as the median-tier predictions since the Llama outcome defines that tier now. For the remaining experiments like exp-021, I'll generate full median-tier forecasts. Now I'll organize everything by plan_id and generate the YAML output.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34018,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34018},"output_tokens":22,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01bac97f-9e4c-4f66-82dd-9e96536b0654","uuid":"d0dc8df5-5b35-4d1c-81aa-c6ea24629d5b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01C6jnynmsXUdXE4wsMAQAbk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: |\n  Scenario A 主导：Llama-70B verbosity 显著（BT ~65%）但 formality NS（BT ~55%）。\n  C3 降级为 \"2/3 target judges show formality bias; susceptibility is architecture-dependent\"。\n  Llama formality 作为 partial negative case——非所有架构对所有轴均敏感，增加论文 nuance。\n  Verbosity 仍有三架构支撑（GPT-4o 76%、Qwen3 77%、Llama ~65%），core claim 不动。\n  Per-axis confound structure (C2b) 在 Llama 上复现：verbosity pure pattern 成立（Style OR sig, Orig OR NS）。\n  MF1 第5层（Llama independent architecture）部分成立——verbosity ✓, formality ✗。\n  降级为 \"4.5/5 layers holding\"，§6 新增 architecture-dependent susceptibility + formality generalizability 两段。\n  n_biased_target_judges = 2 (formality) / 3 (verbosity)。\n  预期 reviewer score 3.5–4.0，Findings 保底，Main 需要 framing 到位。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: \"在 Claude Sonnet 和第三方 judge 上复制 formality pairwise 实验。项目演化后实际执行了 Claude Sonnet（负控制）+ Qwen3-32B + Llama-70B。\"\n    expected_results:\n      claude_bt_formality: 0.562\n      claude_bt_formality_p: 0.091\n      claude_bt_formality_ci: [0.489, 0.636]\n      qwen32b_bt_formality: 0.665\n      qwen32b_bt_formality_p: 0.0001\n      llama_bt_formality: 0.553\n      llama_bt_formality_p: 0.21\n      llama_bt_formality_ci: [0.476, 0.630]\n      n_judges_formality_sig: 2\n      judges_formality_sig: [\"GPT-4o\", \"Qwen3-32B\"]\n      judges_formality_ns: [\"Claude Sonnet\", \"Llama-70B\"]\n    result_rationale: |\n      Claude 已实测为负控制（BT 56.2% NS）。Qwen3-32B 已实测为正（BT 66.5%）。\n      Llama-70B 在 median 档 formality BT 落在 52–60% 区间。Rationale：Llama 架构对\n      formality 的内在偏好弱于 GPT-4o/Qwen3。Llama 训练数据中 formal/casual 文本分布\n      可能更均衡（Meta 训练语料偏 web-crawl，formal/casual 比例接近），导致 formality\n      维度上不产生系统性偏好。这与 verbosity 不同——verbosity 偏好是跨架构的 RLHF 副\n      产品（所有 chat model 均经历 \"详细回答 > 简短回答\" 的 reward signal）。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: Formality BT across judges (LLMBar)\"\n        rows:\n          - judge: \"GPT-4o\"\n            bt: 0.630\n            ci: \"[0.558, 0.703]\"\n            p: \"<0.001\"\n            sig: \"***\"\n          - judge: \"Qwen3-32B\"\n            bt: 0.665\n            ci: \"[0.585, 0.739]\"\n            p: \"<0.0001\"\n            sig: \"****\"\n          - judge: \"Llama-70B\"\n            bt: 0.553\n            ci: \"[0.476, 0.630]\"\n            p: \"0.21\"\n            sig: \"NS\"\n          - judge: \"Claude Sonnet\"\n            bt: 0.562\n            ci: \"[0.489, 0.636]\"\n            p: \"0.091\"\n            sig: \"NS\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: 4 judges × formality BT with 95% CI. GPT-4o 和 Qwen3-32B CI 不包含 0.50；Llama 和 Claude CI 包含 0.50。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Formality bias 是 architecture-dependent：GPT-4o/Qwen3-32B 显著，Llama/Claude 不显著。\n      这不削弱 C2a（Blindspot 在 biased judges 上仍成立），但要求 C3 表述为\n      \"CSD diagnoses per-judge susceptibility\" 而非 \"all judges are biased\"。\n      Llama formality NS 实际增加了论文可信度——说明 CSD 不是万能 false-positive 机器。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: \"CSD pipeline 在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 上运行 formality counterfactuals。GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B 作为 judges。\"\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_bt: 0.727\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_p: 0.0001\n      gpt4o_mtbench_bt: 0.692\n      gpt4o_mtbench_p: 0.0001\n      qwen32b_alpacaeval_bt: 0.657\n      qwen32b_alpacaeval_p: 0.0001\n      qwen32b_mtbench_bt: 0.712\n      qwen32b_mtbench_p: 0.0001\n      llama_alpacaeval_bt: 0.54\n      llama_alpacaeval_p: 0.28\n      llama_mtbench_bt: 0.52\n      llama_mtbench_p: 0.55\n      cross_benchmark_consistent: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      GPT-4o 跨 benchmark 结果已实测（AlpacaEval 72.7%、MT-Bench 69.2%）。Qwen3 在\n      AlpacaEval/MT-Bench 上预期与 LLMBar 趋势一致（±5pp 波动，benchmark 难度和文本\n      特征差异导致）。Llama 在 median 档 formality 跨 benchmark 均 NS——如果 LLMBar\n      上 NS，其他 benchmark 也不会突然显著，因为 Llama 架构本身对 formality 不敏感。\n      MT-Bench 是个例外场景：GPT-4o Likert 在 MT-Bench 上边际显著（p=0.016），但这\n      是因为 MT-Bench 文本更长、Likert 评分方差更大，不改变跨 benchmark 的基本模式。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: Formality BT across benchmarks × judges\"\n        rows:\n          - benchmark: \"LLMBar\"\n            gpt4o: \"63.0%***\"\n            qwen32b: \"66.5%****\"\n            llama: \"55.3% NS\"\n          - benchmark: \"AlpacaEval\"\n            gpt4o: \"72.7%****\"\n            qwen32b: \"65.7%****\"\n            llama: \"54.0% NS\"\n          - benchmark: \"MT-Bench\"\n            gpt4o: \"69.2%****\"\n            qwen32b: \"71.2%****\"\n            llama: \"52.0% NS\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: 3 benchmarks × 4 judges, 色深度 = BT win probability。Llama 列整体浅色。\"\n    analysis: |\n      跨 benchmark 一致性强化了两个结论：(1) formality bias 在 GPT-4o/Qwen3 上是稳健的，\n      不依赖特定 benchmark；(2) Llama formality NS 也是稳健的，不是 LLMBar 特有现象。\n      这排除了 \"Llama 在 LLMBar 上碰巧 NS\" 的解释。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: \"每个 judge × benchmark × axis 组合同时计算 Likert ATE 和 BT，系统比较测量敏感度。\"\n    expected_results:\n      total_cells: 18\n      bt_significant_cells: 10\n      likert_significant_cells: 1\n      both_significant_cells: 1\n      blindspot_rate: 0.90\n      sole_exception: \"GPT-4o × MT-Bench × formality (Likert d=0.167 p=0.016)\"\n      verbosity_likert_all_ns: true\n      formality_likert_all_ns_except_mtbench: true\n      llama_formality_bt_ns: true\n      llama_verbosity_bt_sig_likert_ns: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      已有实测数据覆盖大部分 cells。Likert 仅在 MT-Bench formality 上显著（d=0.167），\n      其余 17/18 cells 中 Likert 均 NS。原因：Likert 的 tie-heavy 分布（tie rate\n      43–73%）系统性地压缩了效应量。MT-Bench 例外是因为其文本较长，Likert 评分方差更大\n      （tie rate 较低），恰好突破了检测阈值。但即便在 MT-Bench 上，BT 效应也远强于\n      Likert（BT 69.2% vs Likert d=0.167）。Llama verbosity 是新的 Blindspot cell：\n      BT ~65% sig 但 Likert NS，进一步确认 Blindspot 不限于 GPT-4o/Qwen3。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: Sensitivity comparison — BT significant vs Likert significant\"\n        rows:\n          - cell: \"GPT-4o × LLMBar × formality\"\n            bt: \"63.0%***\"\n            likert: \"d=-0.07 NS\"\n            blindspot: \"Yes\"\n          - cell: \"GPT-4o × LLMBar × verbosity\"\n            bt: \"76.0%****\"\n            likert: \"d=0.08 NS\"\n            blindspot: \"Yes\"\n          - cell: \"GPT-4o × MT-Bench × formality\"\n            bt: \"69.2%****\"\n            likert: \"d=0.17*\"\n            blindspot: \"No\"\n          - cell: \"Qwen3 × LLMBar × formality\"\n            bt: \"66.5%****\"\n            likert: \"d=0.01 NS\"\n            blindspot: \"Yes\"\n          - cell: \"Qwen3 × LLMBar × verbosity\"\n            bt: \"77.3%****\"\n            likert: \"d=-0.15 NS\"\n            blindspot: \"Yes\"\n          - cell: \"Llama × LLMBar × verbosity\"\n            bt: \"65.0%**\"\n            likert: \"d=0.08 NS\"\n            blindspot: \"Yes\"\n          - cell: \"Llama × LLMBar × formality\"\n            bt: \"55.3% NS\"\n            likert: \"d=0.03 NS\"\n            blindspot: \"N/A (BT also NS)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: x = BT win probability, y = Likert Cohen's d. 对角线上如果两者一致应正相关；实际数据显示 BT 有大效应而 Likert d ≈ 0 的系统偏离。\"\n    analysis: |\n      9/10 个 BT-significant cells 中 Likert 均 NS，Blindspot rate 90%。唯一例外\n      （MT-Bench formality d=0.167）效应量仍小于 BT 等价效应量的 1/4。这证明\n      measurement mode 是 dominant factor——不是某个 judge 或 benchmark 的特例，\n      而是 Likert 作为测量工具的系统性缺陷。\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: \"原始文本 vs 双重改写文本的 pairwise 比较，量化与风格无关的改写偏好 artifact。扩展到所有 judge × axis 组合。\"\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_formality_bt_p_original: 0.418\n      gpt4o_formality_p: 0.037\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_p_original: 0.167\n      gpt4o_verbosity_p: 0.0001\n      qwen32b_formality_bt_p_original: 0.377\n      qwen32b_formality_p: 0.0006\n      qwen32b_verbosity_bt_p_original: 0.082\n      qwen32b_verbosity_p: 0.0001\n      llama_formality_bt_p_original: 0.42\n      llama_formality_p: 0.06\n      llama_verbosity_bt_p_original: 0.25\n      llama_verbosity_p: 0.0001\n      artifact_confirmed: true\n      gee_controls_for_it: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      GPT-4o 和 Qwen3 实测结果已确认改写 artifact 存在（judges 系统性偏好 LLM-polished\n      text over original）。Llama 在 median 档预期类似模式但弱化：formality placebo BT\n      ~42%（边际），verbosity placebo BT ~25%（显著）。原因：所有 RLHF-trained judges\n      共享对 polished text 的偏好，但强度因架构而异。关键：GEE Orig OR 已控制此 artifact，\n      verbosity Orig OR NS 证明 style effect 未被 artifact 污染。Llama placebo 数据\n      补完第三架构，但不改变结论——artifact 是 GEE 已知且已控制的 confound。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: 3 judges × 2 axes, placebo BT P(original)。所有 bar 低于 50% = judges 偏好 DR。Verbosity artifact 更强。\"\n    analysis: |\n      改写 artifact 跨架构一致。但这恰恰验证了 GEE decomposition 的必要性：\n      verbosity Orig OR NS 说明 style OR 未被 artifact 膨胀。\n      Formality Orig OR significant = style effect 和 artifact 交织，需 GEE 分离。\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: \"将 Qwen3-32B formality 从 n=100 扩展到 n=355（NLI-pass）。验证效应稳定性，收窄 CI。\"\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 400\n      n_nli_pass: 355\n      nli_pass_rate: 0.888\n      bt_p_formal: 0.675\n      bt_ci: [0.637, 0.713]\n      bt_ci_width_pp: 7.6\n      bt_p: 0.0001\n      likert_ate: -0.059\n      likert_p: 0.5999\n      likert_d: -0.025\n      gee_style_or: 2.15\n      gee_style_p: 0.0001\n      gee_orig_or: 4.99\n      gee_orig_p: 0.0001\n      vs_n100_bt_delta_pp: 1.0\n      vs_n100_ci_improvement: \"2x narrower\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      实测结果：BT 67.5% [63.7%, 71.3%] 与 n=100 时 66.5% [58.5%, 73.9%] 一致（Δ=+1.0pp），\n      CI 从 15.4pp 收窄到 7.6pp。Likert d=-0.025 仍完全 NS（p=0.60）。这是 bootstrap\n      attenuation curve 的实验确认：n 增大只收窄 CI，不改变 d ≈ 0 的点估计。\n      GEE Style OR 从 4.20 降到 2.15 是因为 n=400 样本中 originality confound 分布\n      更均匀，Style 和 Orig 效应更清晰地分离。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: n=100 vs n=355 comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - metric: \"BT P(formal)\"\n            n100: \"66.5% [58.5, 73.9]\"\n            n355: \"67.5% [63.7, 71.3]\"\n          - metric: \"Likert d\"\n            n100: \"0.012\"\n            n355: \"-0.025\"\n          - metric: \"GEE Style OR\"\n            n100: \"4.20\"\n            n355: \"2.15\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"已有 bootstrap attenuation curve figure：d_median flat at -0.017 across n=50→355。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Scaled replication 确认三点：(1) BT 效应稳定（非 small-n artifact），\n      (2) Likert Blindspot 在大样本下持续（排除 power gap 解释），\n      (3) bootstrap attenuation curve 是 smoking gun——d ≈ 0 是 Likert 的结构性上限。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: \"使用 GPT-4o 作为 rewriter 替代 Qwen3-32B，在 formality 和 verbosity 上比较结果。排除 Qwen-family artifact。\"\n    expected_results:\n      formality_gpt4o_rewriter_bt: 0.644\n      formality_gpt4o_rewriter_ci: [0.561, 0.728]\n      formality_baseline_qwen3_bt: 0.665\n      formality_delta_pp: -2.1\n      formality_ci_overlap: true\n      verbosity_gpt4o_rewriter_bt: 0.735\n      verbosity_gpt4o_rewriter_ci: [0.654, 0.809]\n      verbosity_baseline_qwen3_bt: 0.773\n      verbosity_delta_pp: -3.8\n      verbosity_ci_overlap: true\n      rewriter_independent: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      实测结果：GPT-4o rewriter formality 64.4% vs Qwen3 rewriter 66.5%（Δ=-2.1pp，\n      CI 重叠）；verbosity 73.5% vs 77.3%（Δ=-3.8pp，CI 重叠）。两个 rewriter 产生\n      统计不可区分的结果，说明检测到的 bias 来自 judge 而非 rewriter。\n      GPT-4o rewriter NLI pass rate（formality 90%, verbosity 81%）与 Qwen3（88%, 86%）\n      可比，排除了 rewriter 质量差异的解释。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: Rewriter independence (Qwen3 vs GPT-4o rewriter)\"\n        rows:\n          - axis: \"Formality\"\n            qwen3_rewriter: \"66.5% [58.5, 73.9]\"\n            gpt4o_rewriter: \"64.4% [56.1, 72.8]\"\n            delta: \"-2.1pp\"\n            overlap: \"Yes\"\n          - axis: \"Verbosity\"\n            qwen3_rewriter: \"77.3% [70.3, 84.3]\"\n            gpt4o_rewriter: \"73.5% [65.4, 80.9]\"\n            delta: \"-3.8pp\"\n            overlap: \"Yes\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      Rewriter independence 是 CSD pipeline 的核心假设之一。实测结果排除了\n      \"Qwen3-32B rewriter 引入 systematic artifact that only Qwen3 judge detects\"\n      的循环依赖假设。两个不同架构家族的 rewriter 产生一致结果 = bias 在 judge 端。\n\n  - name: \"GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring (API)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-020\"\n    description: \"GPT-4o API 在 verbosity 和 register counterfactual pairs 上的 pairwise + Likert 评分。\"\n    expected_results:\n      verbosity_bt: 0.760\n      verbosity_bt_ci: [0.688, 0.828]\n      verbosity_bt_p: 0.0001\n      verbosity_likert_ate: 0.116\n      verbosity_likert_p: 0.403\n      verbosity_likert_d: 0.078\n      verbosity_gee_style_or: 10.97\n      verbosity_gee_orig_or: 0.437\n      verbosity_gee_orig_p: 0.051\n      verbosity_blindspot: true\n      register_bt: 0.570\n      register_bt_ci: [0.500, 0.640]\n      register_bt_p: 0.04\n      register_likert_ate: 0.0\n      register_likert_p: 0.785\n      register_gee_style_or: 1.876\n      register_gee_orig_or: 2.210\n      register_blindspot: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      实测结果。Verbosity BT 76.0% 与 Qwen3 77.3% 高度一致——verbosity bias 跨架构\n      稳定。GEE Style OR=10.97 确认 pure style pattern（Orig OR NS）。Likert ATE=+0.12\n      方向正确但 p=0.40 完全 NS，Blindspot 确认。Register BT 57.0% 边际显著，\n      GEE 分解后 originality dominant（OR=2.21 > Style OR=1.88），与 Qwen3 register\n      模式一致。两个 judge 在 register 上均显示 originality-dominated pattern。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      GPT-4o verbosity 补完了 Evidence Matrix 的关键 cell。三个结论：\n      (1) Verbosity pure style pattern 跨 GPT-4o/Qwen3 一致（OR 11 vs 13）。\n      (2) Register originality-dominated pattern 跨 judge 一致。\n      (3) Verbosity Likert Blindspot 在 GPT-4o 上也成立（d=0.078 NS vs BT 76%）。\n\n  - name: \"Third target judge — Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-021\"\n    description: \"Llama-3.3-70B 作为第三个 target judge，在 LLMBar verbosity + formality 上运行完整 CSD pipeline（pairwise BT + Likert + GEE decomposition）。\"\n    expected_results:\n      # Verbosity — significant, median range\n      verbosity_bt: 0.652\n      verbosity_bt_ci: [0.572, 0.728]\n      verbosity_bt_p: 0.0003\n      verbosity_likert_ate: 0.085\n      verbosity_likert_p: 0.46\n      verbosity_likert_d: 0.082\n      verbosity_likert_tie_rate: 0.61\n      verbosity_blindspot: true\n      verbosity_consistency_rate: 0.67\n      verbosity_gee_style_or: 5.48\n      verbosity_gee_style_ci: [2.31, 13.0]\n      verbosity_gee_style_p: 0.0001\n      verbosity_gee_orig_or: 0.62\n      verbosity_gee_orig_ci: [0.27, 1.42]\n      verbosity_gee_orig_p: 0.26\n      verbosity_direction_verbose_to_concise_pref: 0.72\n      verbosity_direction_concise_to_verbose_pref: 0.83\n      # Formality — NS, median range\n      formality_bt: 0.553\n      formality_bt_ci: [0.476, 0.630]\n      formality_bt_p: 0.21\n      formality_likert_ate: 0.025\n      formality_likert_p: 0.82\n      formality_likert_d: 0.023\n      formality_likert_tie_rate: 0.70\n      formality_blindspot: false  # BT also NS → not a blindspot, just no bias\n      formality_consistency_rate: 0.58\n      formality_gee_style_or: 1.35\n      formality_gee_style_ci: [0.71, 2.57]\n      formality_gee_style_p: 0.36\n      formality_gee_orig_or: 3.82\n      formality_gee_orig_ci: [1.92, 7.60]\n      formality_gee_orig_p: 0.0001\n      formality_direction_formal_to_casual_win: 0.62\n      formality_direction_casual_to_formal_win: 0.48\n      # Summary\n      n_pairs_verbosity: 86\n      n_pairs_formality: 88\n      biased_axes: [\"verbosity\"]\n      unbiased_axes: [\"formality\"]\n    result_rationale: |\n      Verbosity BT 65.2%：Llama 检测到 verbose 偏好，但弱于 GPT-4o（76%）和 Qwen3（77%）。\n      原因：Llama-3.3 的 RLHF 训练使用 Meta 内部 reward model，其 verbosity reward\n      信号可能弱于 GPT-4o/Qwen3 的训练信号，但方向一致——所有 chat RLHF 都隐含\n      \"更详细 = 更好\"。GEE verbosity Style OR=5.48（vs GPT-4o 10.97, Qwen3 13.10）\n      确认 pure style pattern：Orig OR NS，风格效应独立于改写 artifact。这是 C2b\n      per-axis confound structure 在第三架构上的复现。\n\n      Formality BT 55.3%：Llama 对 formality 没有统计显著偏好。原因：formality 偏好\n      是 architecture-specific 的。GPT-4o 和 Qwen3 的 system prompt/RLHF 倾向于\n      formal 输出风格（OpenAI 和 Alibaba 的 alignment 偏好），而 Llama 的 alignment\n      更中性。GEE 分解揭示 formality Style OR=1.35 NS 但 Orig OR=3.82 sig——\n      judges 偏好原始文本（改写 artifact），但没有方向性 formality 偏好。\n      这与 Claude 负控制模式不同（Claude Style OR=1.47 NS, Orig OR=6.66 sig）：\n      Claude 完全无偏，Llama formality 仅仅是边际——BT 55.3% 方向正确但 power 不足。\n\n      Likert 在两轴均 NS（formality d=0.023, verbosity d=0.082），但 verbosity\n      BT 显著 → Blindspot 在 Llama 上也成立。这是 median 档的核心贡献：\n      第三架构确认 verbosity Blindspot，同时 formality NS 增加了 nuance。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: Llama-70B CSD results (LLMBar)\"\n        rows:\n          - axis: \"Verbosity\"\n            bt: \"65.2% [57.2, 72.8]\"\n            bt_p: \"0.0003\"\n            likert_d: \"0.082\"\n            likert_p: \"0.46\"\n            gee_style_or: \"5.48***\"\n            gee_orig_or: \"0.62 NS\"\n            pattern: \"Pure style\"\n            blindspot: \"Yes\"\n          - axis: \"Formality\"\n            bt: \"55.3% [47.6, 63.0]\"\n            bt_p: \"0.21\"\n            likert_d: \"0.023\"\n            likert_p: \"0.82\"\n            gee_style_or: \"1.35 NS\"\n            gee_orig_or: \"3.82***\"\n            pattern: \"Originality only\"\n            blindspot: \"N/A\"\n      - caption: \"Table: Updated Evidence Matrix — all 4 judges × 2 axes\"\n        rows:\n          - judge: \"GPT-4o\"\n            verbosity_bt: \"76.0%****\"\n            verbosity_gee_pattern: \"Pure style (OR=10.97)\"\n            formality_bt: \"63.0%***\"\n            formality_gee_pattern: \"Conditional (OR=2.21)\"\n          - judge: \"Qwen3-32B\"\n            verbosity_bt: \"77.3%****\"\n            verbosity_gee_pattern: \"Pure style (OR=13.10)\"\n            formality_bt: \"66.5%****\"\n            formality_gee_pattern: \"Conditional (OR=4.20)\"\n          - judge: \"Llama-70B\"\n            verbosity_bt: \"65.2%***\"\n            verbosity_gee_pattern: \"Pure style (OR=5.48)\"\n            formality_bt: \"55.3% NS\"\n            formality_gee_pattern: \"Originality only (OR=1.35 NS)\"\n          - judge: \"Claude Sonnet\"\n            verbosity_bt: \"54.1% NS\"\n            verbosity_gee_pattern: \"None (OR=1.52 NS)\"\n            formality_bt: \"56.2% NS\"\n            formality_gee_pattern: \"None (OR=1.47 NS)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: 4 judges × verbosity BT。三个 target judges（GPT-4o, Qwen3, Llama）CI 不包含 50%，Claude CI 包含 50%。Llama 效应弱于 GPT-4o/Qwen3 但方向一致。\"\n      - \"Forest plot: 4 judges × formality BT。仅 GPT-4o/Qwen3 CI 不包含 50%。Llama 和 Claude 均 NS。\"\n      - \"GEE OR comparison: 3 judges × verbosity。Style OR 梯度 Qwen3 13.1 > GPT-4o 11.0 > Llama 5.5，Orig OR 全部 NS。Per-axis confound pattern 跨架构复现。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Llama 结果构成 median 档的核心叙事：\n      (1) Verbosity bias 三架构确认（3/3 target judges sig）。GEE pure style pattern\n          也三架构复现（Orig OR NS in all three）。这是 C2b 最强证据。\n      (2) Formality bias 仅 2/3 target judges sig。C3 需要调整：\n          \"CSD reveals architecture-dependent susceptibility—GPT-4o and Qwen3-32B\n          show significant formality bias while Llama-70B does not, suggesting that\n          formality preference is shaped by model-specific alignment rather than being\n          an inherent property of pairwise evaluation.\"\n      (3) MF1 第5层（Llama）部分成立：verbosity ✓ formality ✗。\n          不能说 \"5 independent controls all hold\"，改为\n          \"five controls, four of which hold fully; the fifth (Llama replication)\n          holds for verbosity but not formality, consistent with architecture-dependent\n          susceptibility.\"\n      (4) Llama formality 不是负控制（Claude 是负控制——两轴均 NS）。\n          Llama 是 partial case：一轴 sig 一轴 NS = axis-dependent + architecture-dependent\n          交互。这比简单的 \"all judges biased\" 更有趣，也更可信。\n\n  - name: \"Double-rewrite placebo BT (anti-amplification control)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-022\"\n    description: \"原始文本 vs 双重改写文本的 BT 比较，量化 format-level amplification 风险。GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B + Llama。\"\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_formality_bt_p_orig: 0.418\n      gpt4o_formality_p: 0.037\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_p_orig: 0.167\n      gpt4o_verbosity_p: 0.0001\n      qwen32b_formality_bt_p_orig: 0.377\n      qwen32b_formality_p: 0.0006\n      qwen32b_verbosity_bt_p_orig: 0.082\n      qwen32b_verbosity_p: 0.0001\n      llama_formality_bt_p_orig: 0.425\n      llama_formality_p: 0.08\n      llama_verbosity_bt_p_orig: 0.22\n      llama_verbosity_p: 0.0001\n      artifact_direction: \"DR preferred over original (all judges, all axes)\"\n      gee_controls_for_it: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      GPT-4o 和 Qwen3 实测结果已确认。Llama placebo预期：formality P(orig)≈42.5%\n      （弱于 Qwen3 的 37.7%，因 Llama 对 formality 整体不敏感所以 artifact 也弱），\n      verbosity P(orig)≈22%（verbosity artifact 仍强因为 RLHF 普遍偏好 verbose content）。\n      关键论点不变：artifact 存在 → GEE Orig OR 已控制 → verbosity Orig OR NS = pure style。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      Llama placebo 补完第三架构。三个 judges 均偏好 DR over original，确认改写\n      artifact 是 universal phenomenon。但 GEE 已经控制了它，verbosity 结论不受影响。\n\n  - name: \"NLI gate ablation (content-mediated signal quantification)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-023\"\n    description: \"NLI-pass vs NLI-fail pairs 的 BT 比较，量化 content-mediated signal 比例。\"\n    expected_results:\n      formality_nli_pass_bt: 0.665\n      formality_nli_pass_p: 0.0001\n      formality_nli_fail_bt: 0.417\n      formality_nli_fail_p: 0.69\n      formality_nli_fail_n: 12\n      verbosity_nli_pass_bt: 0.773\n      verbosity_nli_pass_p: 0.0001\n      verbosity_nli_fail_bt: 0.750\n      verbosity_nli_fail_p: 0.006\n      verbosity_nli_fail_n: 14\n      llama_formality_nli_fail_bt: 0.44\n      llama_formality_nli_fail_note: \"n≈12, too small for reliable estimate\"\n      llama_verbosity_nli_fail_bt: 0.68\n      llama_verbosity_nli_fail_note: \"still significant, consistent with pure style\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Qwen3 实测结果（formality NLI-fail BT reversal to 41.7%，verbosity NLI-fail\n      stable at 75%）是 MF1 Layer 1 的核心证据。NLI-fail formality pairs 中内容差异\n      主导 → 移除 NLI gate 后 formal preference 消失甚至反转（judges 偏好实际内容\n      更好的那个，碰巧是 casual 方向）。Verbosity NLI-fail 仍强 → style bias 太强，\n      即使内容有差异也压不住。Llama 在 median 档的 NLI-fail 结果应与 Qwen3 一致\n      （方向相同），但因 Llama formality 本身 NS，NLI-fail reversal 不显著。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      NLI gate ablation 是最强 anti-amplification 证据。如果 pairwise 格式放大偏差，\n      移除 NLI gate 应进一步放大——但 formality 反而反转。这证明 NLI gate 清除\n      content noise，不放大 style signal。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-axis gradient formalization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-024\"\n    description: \"NLI rejection rate（操纵侵入性代理）vs BT 的跨轴梯度，定性 anti-amplification 论证。\"\n    expected_results:\n      register_nli_rejection: 0.06\n      register_bt: 0.553\n      formality_nli_rejection: 0.12\n      formality_bt: 0.665\n      verbosity_nli_rejection: 0.14\n      verbosity_bt: 0.773\n      correlation_direction: \"positive\"\n      n_points: 3\n    result_rationale: |\n      实测结果。三轴形成正梯度：register（低侵入 6%→弱 BT 55%）< formality（中侵入\n      12%→中 BT 67%）< verbosity（高侵入 14%→强 BT 77%）。如果 pairwise 格式统一\n      放大偏差，三轴应显示相似 BT（因为格式相同）。但 BT 与操纵侵入性正相关，\n      说明检测到的信号大小与实际操纵强度匹配——即 detection 而非 amplification。\n      仅 3 个数据点，定性论证，不做统计检验。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter: x = NLI rejection rate, y = BT。3 点 + 趋势线。定性正相关。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cross-axis gradient 是 §5.2 中的定性 supporting evidence，3 点不足以做统计推断。\n      但方向一致性增加了 anti-amplification 论证的整体可信度。与 NLI ablation 和\n      Claude negative control 形成三层 converging evidence。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34018,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34018},"output_tokens":22,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01bac97f-9e4c-4f66-82dd-9e96536b0654","uuid":"adb17e21-bae8-48c7-85c3-3285e3671def"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":294861,"duration_api_ms":296791,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: |\n  Scenario A 主导：Llama-70B verbosity 显著（BT ~65%）但 formality NS（BT ~55%）。\n  C3 降级为 \"2/3 target judges show formality bias; susceptibility is architecture-dependent\"。\n  Llama formality 作为 partial negative case——非所有架构对所有轴均敏感，增加论文 nuance。\n  Verbosity 仍有三架构支撑（GPT-4o 76%、Qwen3 77%、Llama ~65%），core claim 不动。\n  Per-axis confound structure (C2b) 在 Llama 上复现：verbosity pure pattern 成立（Style OR sig, Orig OR NS）。\n  MF1 第5层（Llama independent architecture）部分成立——verbosity ✓, formality ✗。\n  降级为 \"4.5/5 layers holding\"，§6 新增 architecture-dependent susceptibility + formality generalizability 两段。\n  n_biased_target_judges = 2 (formality) / 3 (verbosity)。\n  预期 reviewer score 3.5–4.0，Findings 保底，Main 需要 framing 到位。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: \"在 Claude Sonnet 和第三方 judge 上复制 formality pairwise 实验。项目演化后实际执行了 Claude Sonnet（负控制）+ Qwen3-32B + Llama-70B。\"\n    expected_results:\n      claude_bt_formality: 0.562\n      claude_bt_formality_p: 0.091\n      claude_bt_formality_ci: [0.489, 0.636]\n      qwen32b_bt_formality: 0.665\n      qwen32b_bt_formality_p: 0.0001\n      llama_bt_formality: 0.553\n      llama_bt_formality_p: 0.21\n      llama_bt_formality_ci: [0.476, 0.630]\n      n_judges_formality_sig: 2\n      judges_formality_sig: [\"GPT-4o\", \"Qwen3-32B\"]\n      judges_formality_ns: [\"Claude Sonnet\", \"Llama-70B\"]\n    result_rationale: |\n      Claude 已实测为负控制（BT 56.2% NS）。Qwen3-32B 已实测为正（BT 66.5%）。\n      Llama-70B 在 median 档 formality BT 落在 52–60% 区间。Rationale：Llama 架构对\n      formality 的内在偏好弱于 GPT-4o/Qwen3。Llama 训练数据中 formal/casual 文本分布\n      可能更均衡（Meta 训练语料偏 web-crawl，formal/casual 比例接近），导致 formality\n      维度上不产生系统性偏好。这与 verbosity 不同——verbosity 偏好是跨架构的 RLHF 副\n      产品（所有 chat model 均经历 \"详细回答 > 简短回答\" 的 reward signal）。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: Formality BT across judges (LLMBar)\"\n        rows:\n          - judge: \"GPT-4o\"\n            bt: 0.630\n            ci: \"[0.558, 0.703]\"\n            p: \"<0.001\"\n            sig: \"***\"\n          - judge: \"Qwen3-32B\"\n            bt: 0.665\n            ci: \"[0.585, 0.739]\"\n            p: \"<0.0001\"\n            sig: \"****\"\n          - judge: \"Llama-70B\"\n            bt: 0.553\n            ci: \"[0.476, 0.630]\"\n            p: \"0.21\"\n            sig: \"NS\"\n          - judge: \"Claude Sonnet\"\n            bt: 0.562\n            ci: \"[0.489, 0.636]\"\n            p: \"0.091\"\n            sig: \"NS\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: 4 judges × formality BT with 95% CI. GPT-4o 和 Qwen3-32B CI 不包含 0.50；Llama 和 Claude CI 包含 0.50。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Formality bias 是 architecture-dependent：GPT-4o/Qwen3-32B 显著，Llama/Claude 不显著。\n      这不削弱 C2a（Blindspot 在 biased judges 上仍成立），但要求 C3 表述为\n      \"CSD diagnoses per-judge susceptibility\" 而非 \"all judges are biased\"。\n      Llama formality NS 实际增加了论文可信度——说明 CSD 不是万能 false-positive 机器。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: \"CSD pipeline 在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 上运行 formality counterfactuals。GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B 作为 judges。\"\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_bt: 0.727\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_p: 0.0001\n      gpt4o_mtbench_bt: 0.692\n      gpt4o_mtbench_p: 0.0001\n      qwen32b_alpacaeval_bt: 0.657\n      qwen32b_alpacaeval_p: 0.0001\n      qwen32b_mtbench_bt: 0.712\n      qwen32b_mtbench_p: 0.0001\n      llama_alpacaeval_bt: 0.54\n      llama_alpacaeval_p: 0.28\n      llama_mtbench_bt: 0.52\n      llama_mtbench_p: 0.55\n      cross_benchmark_consistent: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      GPT-4o 跨 benchmark 结果已实测（AlpacaEval 72.7%、MT-Bench 69.2%）。Qwen3 在\n      AlpacaEval/MT-Bench 上预期与 LLMBar 趋势一致（±5pp 波动，benchmark 难度和文本\n      特征差异导致）。Llama 在 median 档 formality 跨 benchmark 均 NS——如果 LLMBar\n      上 NS，其他 benchmark 也不会突然显著，因为 Llama 架构本身对 formality 不敏感。\n      MT-Bench 是个例外场景：GPT-4o Likert 在 MT-Bench 上边际显著（p=0.016），但这\n      是因为 MT-Bench 文本更长、Likert 评分方差更大，不改变跨 benchmark 的基本模式。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: Formality BT across benchmarks × judges\"\n        rows:\n          - benchmark: \"LLMBar\"\n            gpt4o: \"63.0%***\"\n            qwen32b: \"66.5%****\"\n            llama: \"55.3% NS\"\n          - benchmark: \"AlpacaEval\"\n            gpt4o: \"72.7%****\"\n            qwen32b: \"65.7%****\"\n            llama: \"54.0% NS\"\n          - benchmark: \"MT-Bench\"\n            gpt4o: \"69.2%****\"\n            qwen32b: \"71.2%****\"\n            llama: \"52.0% NS\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: 3 benchmarks × 4 judges, 色深度 = BT win probability。Llama 列整体浅色。\"\n    analysis: |\n      跨 benchmark 一致性强化了两个结论：(1) formality bias 在 GPT-4o/Qwen3 上是稳健的，\n      不依赖特定 benchmark；(2) Llama formality NS 也是稳健的，不是 LLMBar 特有现象。\n      这排除了 \"Llama 在 LLMBar 上碰巧 NS\" 的解释。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: \"每个 judge × benchmark × axis 组合同时计算 Likert ATE 和 BT，系统比较测量敏感度。\"\n    expected_results:\n      total_cells: 18\n      bt_significant_cells: 10\n      likert_significant_cells: 1\n      both_significant_cells: 1\n      blindspot_rate: 0.90\n      sole_exception: \"GPT-4o × MT-Bench × formality (Likert d=0.167 p=0.016)\"\n      verbosity_likert_all_ns: true\n      formality_likert_all_ns_except_mtbench: true\n      llama_formality_bt_ns: true\n      llama_verbosity_bt_sig_likert_ns: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      已有实测数据覆盖大部分 cells。Likert 仅在 MT-Bench formality 上显著（d=0.167），\n      其余 17/18 cells 中 Likert 均 NS。原因：Likert 的 tie-heavy 分布（tie rate\n      43–73%）系统性地压缩了效应量。MT-Bench 例外是因为其文本较长，Likert 评分方差更大\n      （tie rate 较低），恰好突破了检测阈值。但即便在 MT-Bench 上，BT 效应也远强于\n      Likert（BT 69.2% vs Likert d=0.167）。Llama verbosity 是新的 Blindspot cell：\n      BT ~65% sig 但 Likert NS，进一步确认 Blindspot 不限于 GPT-4o/Qwen3。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: Sensitivity comparison — BT significant vs Likert significant\"\n        rows:\n          - cell: \"GPT-4o × LLMBar × formality\"\n            bt: \"63.0%***\"\n            likert: \"d=-0.07 NS\"\n            blindspot: \"Yes\"\n          - cell: \"GPT-4o × LLMBar × verbosity\"\n            bt: \"76.0%****\"\n            likert: \"d=0.08 NS\"\n            blindspot: \"Yes\"\n          - cell: \"GPT-4o × MT-Bench × formality\"\n            bt: \"69.2%****\"\n            likert: \"d=0.17*\"\n            blindspot: \"No\"\n          - cell: \"Qwen3 × LLMBar × formality\"\n            bt: \"66.5%****\"\n            likert: \"d=0.01 NS\"\n            blindspot: \"Yes\"\n          - cell: \"Qwen3 × LLMBar × verbosity\"\n            bt: \"77.3%****\"\n            likert: \"d=-0.15 NS\"\n            blindspot: \"Yes\"\n          - cell: \"Llama × LLMBar × verbosity\"\n            bt: \"65.0%**\"\n            likert: \"d=0.08 NS\"\n            blindspot: \"Yes\"\n          - cell: \"Llama × LLMBar × formality\"\n            bt: \"55.3% NS\"\n            likert: \"d=0.03 NS\"\n            blindspot: \"N/A (BT also NS)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: x = BT win probability, y = Likert Cohen's d. 对角线上如果两者一致应正相关；实际数据显示 BT 有大效应而 Likert d ≈ 0 的系统偏离。\"\n    analysis: |\n      9/10 个 BT-significant cells 中 Likert 均 NS，Blindspot rate 90%。唯一例外\n      （MT-Bench formality d=0.167）效应量仍小于 BT 等价效应量的 1/4。这证明\n      measurement mode 是 dominant factor——不是某个 judge 或 benchmark 的特例，\n      而是 Likert 作为测量工具的系统性缺陷。\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: \"原始文本 vs 双重改写文本的 pairwise 比较，量化与风格无关的改写偏好 artifact。扩展到所有 judge × axis 组合。\"\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_formality_bt_p_original: 0.418\n      gpt4o_formality_p: 0.037\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_p_original: 0.167\n      gpt4o_verbosity_p: 0.0001\n      qwen32b_formality_bt_p_original: 0.377\n      qwen32b_formality_p: 0.0006\n      qwen32b_verbosity_bt_p_original: 0.082\n      qwen32b_verbosity_p: 0.0001\n      llama_formality_bt_p_original: 0.42\n      llama_formality_p: 0.06\n      llama_verbosity_bt_p_original: 0.25\n      llama_verbosity_p: 0.0001\n      artifact_confirmed: true\n      gee_controls_for_it: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      GPT-4o 和 Qwen3 实测结果已确认改写 artifact 存在（judges 系统性偏好 LLM-polished\n      text over original）。Llama 在 median 档预期类似模式但弱化：formality placebo BT\n      ~42%（边际），verbosity placebo BT ~25%（显著）。原因：所有 RLHF-trained judges\n      共享对 polished text 的偏好，但强度因架构而异。关键：GEE Orig OR 已控制此 artifact，\n      verbosity Orig OR NS 证明 style effect 未被 artifact 污染。Llama placebo 数据\n      补完第三架构，但不改变结论——artifact 是 GEE 已知且已控制的 confound。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: 3 judges × 2 axes, placebo BT P(original)。所有 bar 低于 50% = judges 偏好 DR。Verbosity artifact 更强。\"\n    analysis: |\n      改写 artifact 跨架构一致。但这恰恰验证了 GEE decomposition 的必要性：\n      verbosity Orig OR NS 说明 style OR 未被 artifact 膨胀。\n      Formality Orig OR significant = style effect 和 artifact 交织，需 GEE 分离。\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: \"将 Qwen3-32B formality 从 n=100 扩展到 n=355（NLI-pass）。验证效应稳定性，收窄 CI。\"\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 400\n      n_nli_pass: 355\n      nli_pass_rate: 0.888\n      bt_p_formal: 0.675\n      bt_ci: [0.637, 0.713]\n      bt_ci_width_pp: 7.6\n      bt_p: 0.0001\n      likert_ate: -0.059\n      likert_p: 0.5999\n      likert_d: -0.025\n      gee_style_or: 2.15\n      gee_style_p: 0.0001\n      gee_orig_or: 4.99\n      gee_orig_p: 0.0001\n      vs_n100_bt_delta_pp: 1.0\n      vs_n100_ci_improvement: \"2x narrower\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      实测结果：BT 67.5% [63.7%, 71.3%] 与 n=100 时 66.5% [58.5%, 73.9%] 一致（Δ=+1.0pp），\n      CI 从 15.4pp 收窄到 7.6pp。Likert d=-0.025 仍完全 NS（p=0.60）。这是 bootstrap\n      attenuation curve 的实验确认：n 增大只收窄 CI，不改变 d ≈ 0 的点估计。\n      GEE Style OR 从 4.20 降到 2.15 是因为 n=400 样本中 originality confound 分布\n      更均匀，Style 和 Orig 效应更清晰地分离。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: n=100 vs n=355 comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - metric: \"BT P(formal)\"\n            n100: \"66.5% [58.5, 73.9]\"\n            n355: \"67.5% [63.7, 71.3]\"\n          - metric: \"Likert d\"\n            n100: \"0.012\"\n            n355: \"-0.025\"\n          - metric: \"GEE Style OR\"\n            n100: \"4.20\"\n            n355: \"2.15\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"已有 bootstrap attenuation curve figure：d_median flat at -0.017 across n=50→355。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Scaled replication 确认三点：(1) BT 效应稳定（非 small-n artifact），\n      (2) Likert Blindspot 在大样本下持续（排除 power gap 解释），\n      (3) bootstrap attenuation curve 是 smoking gun——d ≈ 0 是 Likert 的结构性上限。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: \"使用 GPT-4o 作为 rewriter 替代 Qwen3-32B，在 formality 和 verbosity 上比较结果。排除 Qwen-family artifact。\"\n    expected_results:\n      formality_gpt4o_rewriter_bt: 0.644\n      formality_gpt4o_rewriter_ci: [0.561, 0.728]\n      formality_baseline_qwen3_bt: 0.665\n      formality_delta_pp: -2.1\n      formality_ci_overlap: true\n      verbosity_gpt4o_rewriter_bt: 0.735\n      verbosity_gpt4o_rewriter_ci: [0.654, 0.809]\n      verbosity_baseline_qwen3_bt: 0.773\n      verbosity_delta_pp: -3.8\n      verbosity_ci_overlap: true\n      rewriter_independent: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      实测结果：GPT-4o rewriter formality 64.4% vs Qwen3 rewriter 66.5%（Δ=-2.1pp，\n      CI 重叠）；verbosity 73.5% vs 77.3%（Δ=-3.8pp，CI 重叠）。两个 rewriter 产生\n      统计不可区分的结果，说明检测到的 bias 来自 judge 而非 rewriter。\n      GPT-4o rewriter NLI pass rate（formality 90%, verbosity 81%）与 Qwen3（88%, 86%）\n      可比，排除了 rewriter 质量差异的解释。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: Rewriter independence (Qwen3 vs GPT-4o rewriter)\"\n        rows:\n          - axis: \"Formality\"\n            qwen3_rewriter: \"66.5% [58.5, 73.9]\"\n            gpt4o_rewriter: \"64.4% [56.1, 72.8]\"\n            delta: \"-2.1pp\"\n            overlap: \"Yes\"\n          - axis: \"Verbosity\"\n            qwen3_rewriter: \"77.3% [70.3, 84.3]\"\n            gpt4o_rewriter: \"73.5% [65.4, 80.9]\"\n            delta: \"-3.8pp\"\n            overlap: \"Yes\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      Rewriter independence 是 CSD pipeline 的核心假设之一。实测结果排除了\n      \"Qwen3-32B rewriter 引入 systematic artifact that only Qwen3 judge detects\"\n      的循环依赖假设。两个不同架构家族的 rewriter 产生一致结果 = bias 在 judge 端。\n\n  - name: \"GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring (API)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-020\"\n    description: \"GPT-4o API 在 verbosity 和 register counterfactual pairs 上的 pairwise + Likert 评分。\"\n    expected_results:\n      verbosity_bt: 0.760\n      verbosity_bt_ci: [0.688, 0.828]\n      verbosity_bt_p: 0.0001\n      verbosity_likert_ate: 0.116\n      verbosity_likert_p: 0.403\n      verbosity_likert_d: 0.078\n      verbosity_gee_style_or: 10.97\n      verbosity_gee_orig_or: 0.437\n      verbosity_gee_orig_p: 0.051\n      verbosity_blindspot: true\n      register_bt: 0.570\n      register_bt_ci: [0.500, 0.640]\n      register_bt_p: 0.04\n      register_likert_ate: 0.0\n      register_likert_p: 0.785\n      register_gee_style_or: 1.876\n      register_gee_orig_or: 2.210\n      register_blindspot: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      实测结果。Verbosity BT 76.0% 与 Qwen3 77.3% 高度一致——verbosity bias 跨架构\n      稳定。GEE Style OR=10.97 确认 pure style pattern（Orig OR NS）。Likert ATE=+0.12\n      方向正确但 p=0.40 完全 NS，Blindspot 确认。Register BT 57.0% 边际显著，\n      GEE 分解后 originality dominant（OR=2.21 > Style OR=1.88），与 Qwen3 register\n      模式一致。两个 judge 在 register 上均显示 originality-dominated pattern。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      GPT-4o verbosity 补完了 Evidence Matrix 的关键 cell。三个结论：\n      (1) Verbosity pure style pattern 跨 GPT-4o/Qwen3 一致（OR 11 vs 13）。\n      (2) Register originality-dominated pattern 跨 judge 一致。\n      (3) Verbosity Likert Blindspot 在 GPT-4o 上也成立（d=0.078 NS vs BT 76%）。\n\n  - name: \"Third target judge — Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-021\"\n    description: \"Llama-3.3-70B 作为第三个 target judge，在 LLMBar verbosity + formality 上运行完整 CSD pipeline（pairwise BT + Likert + GEE decomposition）。\"\n    expected_results:\n      # Verbosity — significant, median range\n      verbosity_bt: 0.652\n      verbosity_bt_ci: [0.572, 0.728]\n      verbosity_bt_p: 0.0003\n      verbosity_likert_ate: 0.085\n      verbosity_likert_p: 0.46\n      verbosity_likert_d: 0.082\n      verbosity_likert_tie_rate: 0.61\n      verbosity_blindspot: true\n      verbosity_consistency_rate: 0.67\n      verbosity_gee_style_or: 5.48\n      verbosity_gee_style_ci: [2.31, 13.0]\n      verbosity_gee_style_p: 0.0001\n      verbosity_gee_orig_or: 0.62\n      verbosity_gee_orig_ci: [0.27, 1.42]\n      verbosity_gee_orig_p: 0.26\n      verbosity_direction_verbose_to_concise_pref: 0.72\n      verbosity_direction_concise_to_verbose_pref: 0.83\n      # Formality — NS, median range\n      formality_bt: 0.553\n      formality_bt_ci: [0.476, 0.630]\n      formality_bt_p: 0.21\n      formality_likert_ate: 0.025\n      formality_likert_p: 0.82\n      formality_likert_d: 0.023\n      formality_likert_tie_rate: 0.70\n      formality_blindspot: false  # BT also NS → not a blindspot, just no bias\n      formality_consistency_rate: 0.58\n      formality_gee_style_or: 1.35\n      formality_gee_style_ci: [0.71, 2.57]\n      formality_gee_style_p: 0.36\n      formality_gee_orig_or: 3.82\n      formality_gee_orig_ci: [1.92, 7.60]\n      formality_gee_orig_p: 0.0001\n      formality_direction_formal_to_casual_win: 0.62\n      formality_direction_casual_to_formal_win: 0.48\n      # Summary\n      n_pairs_verbosity: 86\n      n_pairs_formality: 88\n      biased_axes: [\"verbosity\"]\n      unbiased_axes: [\"formality\"]\n    result_rationale: |\n      Verbosity BT 65.2%：Llama 检测到 verbose 偏好，但弱于 GPT-4o（76%）和 Qwen3（77%）。\n      原因：Llama-3.3 的 RLHF 训练使用 Meta 内部 reward model，其 verbosity reward\n      信号可能弱于 GPT-4o/Qwen3 的训练信号，但方向一致——所有 chat RLHF 都隐含\n      \"更详细 = 更好\"。GEE verbosity Style OR=5.48（vs GPT-4o 10.97, Qwen3 13.10）\n      确认 pure style pattern：Orig OR NS，风格效应独立于改写 artifact。这是 C2b\n      per-axis confound structure 在第三架构上的复现。\n\n      Formality BT 55.3%：Llama 对 formality 没有统计显著偏好。原因：formality 偏好\n      是 architecture-specific 的。GPT-4o 和 Qwen3 的 system prompt/RLHF 倾向于\n      formal 输出风格（OpenAI 和 Alibaba 的 alignment 偏好），而 Llama 的 alignment\n      更中性。GEE 分解揭示 formality Style OR=1.35 NS 但 Orig OR=3.82 sig——\n      judges 偏好原始文本（改写 artifact），但没有方向性 formality 偏好。\n      这与 Claude 负控制模式不同（Claude Style OR=1.47 NS, Orig OR=6.66 sig）：\n      Claude 完全无偏，Llama formality 仅仅是边际——BT 55.3% 方向正确但 power 不足。\n\n      Likert 在两轴均 NS（formality d=0.023, verbosity d=0.082），但 verbosity\n      BT 显著 → Blindspot 在 Llama 上也成立。这是 median 档的核心贡献：\n      第三架构确认 verbosity Blindspot，同时 formality NS 增加了 nuance。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table: Llama-70B CSD results (LLMBar)\"\n        rows:\n          - axis: \"Verbosity\"\n            bt: \"65.2% [57.2, 72.8]\"\n            bt_p: \"0.0003\"\n            likert_d: \"0.082\"\n            likert_p: \"0.46\"\n            gee_style_or: \"5.48***\"\n            gee_orig_or: \"0.62 NS\"\n            pattern: \"Pure style\"\n            blindspot: \"Yes\"\n          - axis: \"Formality\"\n            bt: \"55.3% [47.6, 63.0]\"\n            bt_p: \"0.21\"\n            likert_d: \"0.023\"\n            likert_p: \"0.82\"\n            gee_style_or: \"1.35 NS\"\n            gee_orig_or: \"3.82***\"\n            pattern: \"Originality only\"\n            blindspot: \"N/A\"\n      - caption: \"Table: Updated Evidence Matrix — all 4 judges × 2 axes\"\n        rows:\n          - judge: \"GPT-4o\"\n            verbosity_bt: \"76.0%****\"\n            verbosity_gee_pattern: \"Pure style (OR=10.97)\"\n            formality_bt: \"63.0%***\"\n            formality_gee_pattern: \"Conditional (OR=2.21)\"\n          - judge: \"Qwen3-32B\"\n            verbosity_bt: \"77.3%****\"\n            verbosity_gee_pattern: \"Pure style (OR=13.10)\"\n            formality_bt: \"66.5%****\"\n            formality_gee_pattern: \"Conditional (OR=4.20)\"\n          - judge: \"Llama-70B\"\n            verbosity_bt: \"65.2%***\"\n            verbosity_gee_pattern: \"Pure style (OR=5.48)\"\n            formality_bt: \"55.3% NS\"\n            formality_gee_pattern: \"Originality only (OR=1.35 NS)\"\n          - judge: \"Claude Sonnet\"\n            verbosity_bt: \"54.1% NS\"\n            verbosity_gee_pattern: \"None (OR=1.52 NS)\"\n            formality_bt: \"56.2% NS\"\n            formality_gee_pattern: \"None (OR=1.47 NS)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: 4 judges × verbosity BT。三个 target judges（GPT-4o, Qwen3, Llama）CI 不包含 50%，Claude CI 包含 50%。Llama 效应弱于 GPT-4o/Qwen3 但方向一致。\"\n      - \"Forest plot: 4 judges × formality BT。仅 GPT-4o/Qwen3 CI 不包含 50%。Llama 和 Claude 均 NS。\"\n      - \"GEE OR comparison: 3 judges × verbosity。Style OR 梯度 Qwen3 13.1 > GPT-4o 11.0 > Llama 5.5，Orig OR 全部 NS。Per-axis confound pattern 跨架构复现。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Llama 结果构成 median 档的核心叙事：\n      (1) Verbosity bias 三架构确认（3/3 target judges sig）。GEE pure style pattern\n          也三架构复现（Orig OR NS in all three）。这是 C2b 最强证据。\n      (2) Formality bias 仅 2/3 target judges sig。C3 需要调整：\n          \"CSD reveals architecture-dependent susceptibility—GPT-4o and Qwen3-32B\n          show significant formality bias while Llama-70B does not, suggesting that\n          formality preference is shaped by model-specific alignment rather than being\n          an inherent property of pairwise evaluation.\"\n      (3) MF1 第5层（Llama）部分成立：verbosity ✓ formality ✗。\n          不能说 \"5 independent controls all hold\"，改为\n          \"five controls, four of which hold fully; the fifth (Llama replication)\n          holds for verbosity but not formality, consistent with architecture-dependent\n          susceptibility.\"\n      (4) Llama formality 不是负控制（Claude 是负控制——两轴均 NS）。\n          Llama 是 partial case：一轴 sig 一轴 NS = axis-dependent + architecture-dependent\n          交互。这比简单的 \"all judges biased\" 更有趣，也更可信。\n\n  - name: \"Double-rewrite placebo BT (anti-amplification control)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-022\"\n    description: \"原始文本 vs 双重改写文本的 BT 比较，量化 format-level amplification 风险。GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B + Llama。\"\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_formality_bt_p_orig: 0.418\n      gpt4o_formality_p: 0.037\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_p_orig: 0.167\n      gpt4o_verbosity_p: 0.0001\n      qwen32b_formality_bt_p_orig: 0.377\n      qwen32b_formality_p: 0.0006\n      qwen32b_verbosity_bt_p_orig: 0.082\n      qwen32b_verbosity_p: 0.0001\n      llama_formality_bt_p_orig: 0.425\n      llama_formality_p: 0.08\n      llama_verbosity_bt_p_orig: 0.22\n      llama_verbosity_p: 0.0001\n      artifact_direction: \"DR preferred over original (all judges, all axes)\"\n      gee_controls_for_it: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      GPT-4o 和 Qwen3 实测结果已确认。Llama placebo预期：formality P(orig)≈42.5%\n      （弱于 Qwen3 的 37.7%，因 Llama 对 formality 整体不敏感所以 artifact 也弱），\n      verbosity P(orig)≈22%（verbosity artifact 仍强因为 RLHF 普遍偏好 verbose content）。\n      关键论点不变：artifact 存在 → GEE Orig OR 已控制 → verbosity Orig OR NS = pure style。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      Llama placebo 补完第三架构。三个 judges 均偏好 DR over original，确认改写\n      artifact 是 universal phenomenon。但 GEE 已经控制了它，verbosity 结论不受影响。\n\n  - name: \"NLI gate ablation (content-mediated signal quantification)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-023\"\n    description: \"NLI-pass vs NLI-fail pairs 的 BT 比较，量化 content-mediated signal 比例。\"\n    expected_results:\n      formality_nli_pass_bt: 0.665\n      formality_nli_pass_p: 0.0001\n      formality_nli_fail_bt: 0.417\n      formality_nli_fail_p: 0.69\n      formality_nli_fail_n: 12\n      verbosity_nli_pass_bt: 0.773\n      verbosity_nli_pass_p: 0.0001\n      verbosity_nli_fail_bt: 0.750\n      verbosity_nli_fail_p: 0.006\n      verbosity_nli_fail_n: 14\n      llama_formality_nli_fail_bt: 0.44\n      llama_formality_nli_fail_note: \"n≈12, too small for reliable estimate\"\n      llama_verbosity_nli_fail_bt: 0.68\n      llama_verbosity_nli_fail_note: \"still significant, consistent with pure style\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Qwen3 实测结果（formality NLI-fail BT reversal to 41.7%，verbosity NLI-fail\n      stable at 75%）是 MF1 Layer 1 的核心证据。NLI-fail formality pairs 中内容差异\n      主导 → 移除 NLI gate 后 formal preference 消失甚至反转（judges 偏好实际内容\n      更好的那个，碰巧是 casual 方向）。Verbosity NLI-fail 仍强 → style bias 太强，\n      即使内容有差异也压不住。Llama 在 median 档的 NLI-fail 结果应与 Qwen3 一致\n      （方向相同），但因 Llama formality 本身 NS，NLI-fail reversal 不显著。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      NLI gate ablation 是最强 anti-amplification 证据。如果 pairwise 格式放大偏差，\n      移除 NLI gate 应进一步放大——但 formality 反而反转。这证明 NLI gate 清除\n      content noise，不放大 style signal。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-axis gradient formalization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-024\"\n    description: \"NLI rejection rate（操纵侵入性代理）vs BT 的跨轴梯度，定性 anti-amplification 论证。\"\n    expected_results:\n      register_nli_rejection: 0.06\n      register_bt: 0.553\n      formality_nli_rejection: 0.12\n      formality_bt: 0.665\n      verbosity_nli_rejection: 0.14\n      verbosity_bt: 0.773\n      correlation_direction: \"positive\"\n      n_points: 3\n    result_rationale: |\n      实测结果。三轴形成正梯度：register（低侵入 6%→弱 BT 55%）< formality（中侵入\n      12%→中 BT 67%）< verbosity（高侵入 14%→强 BT 77%）。如果 pairwise 格式统一\n      放大偏差，三轴应显示相似 BT（因为格式相同）。但 BT 与操纵侵入性正相关，\n      说明检测到的信号大小与实际操纵强度匹配——即 detection 而非 amplification。\n      仅 3 个数据点，定性论证，不做统计检验。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter: x = NLI rejection rate, y = BT。3 点 + 趋势线。定性正相关。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cross-axis gradient 是 §5.2 中的定性 supporting evidence，3 点不足以做统计推断。\n      但方向一致性增加了 anti-amplification 论证的整体可信度。与 NLI ablation 和\n      Claude negative control 形成三层 converging evidence。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"01bac97f-9e4c-4f66-82dd-9e96536b0654","total_cost_usd":0.6639240000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34018,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":16650,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34018,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":16650,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34018,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34018},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":28976,"outputTokens":31,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.029130999999999997,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":16650,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":34018,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.634793,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"feb3cfe4-aac0-4274-a27a-73e9ff7b6034"}
